From d2b433d5546998e3ce6750fe2e233894d38992f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonas Karlman <jonas@kwiboo.se>
Date: Sat, 11 Apr 2026 14:15:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 159/213] WIP: drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: convert to HDMI bridge
 helpers

Convert dw-hdmi to the DRM HDMI bridge helpers and let the core build
the HDMI infoframes from connector state.

Add AVI, HDMI vendor and HDR DRM infoframe bridge callbacks and keep the
controller-specific byte shuffling in the dw-hdmi driver. Switch the
mode setup to use HDMI connector state for limited range handling and
TMDS character rate, and update the enable path to program infoframes
through drm_atomic_helper_connector_hdmi_update_infoframes().

This makes dw-hdmi behave as a proper HDMI bridge while keeping the
hardware-specific register programming local to the driver.

Signed-off-by: Jonas Karlman <jonas@kwiboo.se>
[chewitt: adapt to the HDMI 2.0 scrambling helpers: advertise HDMI 2.0
 via supported_hdmi_ver, implement the scrambler bridge callbacks and use
 drm_connector_hdmi_{enable,disable}_scrambling(), leaving the 340/600 MHz
 source limits to the core]
